        "message": "LU-20690 tests: read one parity stripe in sanity-ec 312\n\nsanity-ec test_312 read the parity mirror of a 4+2 file through the\nMIRROR scope, expecting a buffered read to be refused with -EINVAL\nand a direct read to succeed.  Once \"ec: store EC parity like\nRAID10\" stores every parity slot as p stripes,\nlov_io_designated_stripe_valid() refuses any read of such a slot that\ndoes not name one of its stripes, so the direct read would fail with\n-EINVAL as well, and the buffered read would be refused for that\nreason rather than for being buffered.\n\nRead stripe 0 of the parity slot through the STRIPE scope in both\ncases, which does not depend on how the parity is stored.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=8\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I85c401147239ee13b3683b747b0edfdaf13ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70571\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Zhenyu Xu <bobijam@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Marc Vef <mvef@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
